; Integer addition — the grammar shared with the @tabnas/parser README,
; where it is also built by hand directly against the engine.
;
; Exercises two dialect features whose whole point is that this grammar
; renders back out of a live engine exactly as written (see
; test/roundtrip.test.js):
;
;   - `NR = <number>` is RFC 5234 prose-val. Prose describes a terminal
;     rather than defining one, which for a built-in lexer token is
;     exactly right: the lexer already supplies `NR`, so the line
;     documents the terminal and compiles to nothing.
;
;   - `PL = "+"` is a production whose whole body is one literal, i.e. a
;     lexical definition. It compiles to the named fixed token `#PL`
;     rather than to a rule, matching the hand-written grammar's
;     `fixed: { token: { '#PL': '+' } }`.
;
; `val` is a pure alias for `add`; it survives compilation rather than
; being inlined away, so it is still a rule (and an AST node) here.
val = add
add = NR [ PL add ]

NR = <number>
PL = "+"
